# SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
#
# DEVELOPMENT ONLY (kpasskeyd --direct-uhid). Gives the user of the *active* local session an ACL on
# /dev/uhid (systemd "uaccess", applied by 73-seat-late.rules), so that
# kpasskeyd can create its virtual FIDO HID device. The ACL moves with the
# foreground session and is removed on logout/user switch.
#
# SECURITY WARNING: /dev/uhid can create ANY HID device, including keyboards
# and mice. Every unsandboxed process of the active user can therefore inject
# input into the session. Production builds replace this with a small
# privileged helper that can only create the fixed FIDO device
# (docs/roadmap.md, phase 2). Do not ship this rule in distribution packages.
KERNEL=="uhid", SUBSYSTEM=="misc", TAG+="uaccess"
